          %p
            In the language of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+theory"} quiver theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representations"} quiver representations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-classification"} A-type
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quivers"} quivers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representation+theory"} quiver representation theory
            the classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel%27s+theorem"} Gabriel theorem
            says (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Gabriel's+theorem#ATypeQuivers"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+object"} indecomposable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representations"} quiver representations
            are still “interval modules”, ie. those for which the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero
            except in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            where they are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+vector+space"} 1-dimensional
            and connected by (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zigzags"} zigzags
            of)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+maps"} identity maps
          %p
            This means that the key property of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+modules"} persistence modules
            – namely that they are entirely characterized by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistence+barcodes"} persistence barcodes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisets"} multisets
            of such intervals – immediately generalizes to zigzag persistence modules.
          %p
            A typical type of a zigzag persistence module appearing in the practice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
            consists of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+groups"} homology groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(X_i)
            of stages
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots \hookrightarrow X_{i - 1} \hookrightarrow X_i \hookrightarrow X_{i + 1} \hookrightarrow \cdots
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtered topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zigzag"} zigzag
            of inclusions into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
