          %p It is claimed (…) that such zigzag persistence modules still retain the same persistent information of interest, but are more robust.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#well_modules Well modules
          %p
            As the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+set"} level
            varies, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+groups"} well groups
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            naturally form a zigzag persistence module, called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+module"} well module
            (Edelsbrunner, Morozov &amp; Patel 2011group#EMP11)).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stability+of+persistence+diagrams"} stability of persistence diagrams
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diamond+principle"} diamond principle
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+group"} well group
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The concept of zigzag persistence modules as a tool in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
            and their relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+representation+theory"} quiver representation theory
            (including a re-proof of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel%27s+theorem"} Gabriel's theorem
            for the case of A-type quivers) is due to:
          %ul
            %li#CarlssonDeSilva10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vin+de+Silva"} Vin de Silva
              = succeed "," do
                %em Zigzag Persistence
              %strong 10
              (2010) 367–405
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0197"} arXiv:0812.0197
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10208-010-9066-0"} doi:10.1007/s10208-010-9066-0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            Application to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+sets"} level sets
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vin+de+Silva"} Vin de Silva
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitriy+Morozov"} Dmitriy Morozov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Zigzag persistent homology and real-valued functions
                %em
                  SCG ‘09: Proceedings of the twenty-fifth annual symposium on Computational geometry (2009) 247–256
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/1542362.1542408"} doi:10.1145/1542362.1542408
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vin+de+Silva"} Vin de Silva
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sara+Kali%C5%A1nik"} Sara Kališnik
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitriy+Morozov"} Dmitriy Morozov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Parametrized Homology via Zigzag Persistence
                %strong 19
                (2019) 657-700
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.03596"} arXiv:1604.03596
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2019.19.657"} doi:10.2140/agt.2019.19.657
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
